lib/features/transaksi/presentation/providers/setoran_refresh.dart<pre><code>/// Reloads every view that shows setoran totals after a setoran changed on
/// the server: Riwayat, and the dashboard, recent activity and nasabah saldo
/// when the pengurus already opened them. Screens never opened are not built.
void reloadAfterSetoranChange(ProviderContainer container) {
  container.read(riwayatAktivitasProvider.notifier).load(silent: true);
  if (container.exists(dashboardProvider)) {
    container.read(dashboardProvider.notifier).loadStats(silent: true);
  }
  if (container.exists(recentActivityProvider)) {
    container.read(recentActivityProvider.notifier).load(silent: true);
  }
  if (container.exists(nasabahProvider)) {
    container.read(nasabahProvider.notifier).loadNasabah(silent: true);
  }
}
</code></pre> <p><code>container.exists</code> is the point: reading a provider that was never built would build it and fire a request for a screen the pengurus never opened. Edit has the same stale-screen gap on <code>staging</code>. Scallss agreed it is a separate follow-up, so it was left out of this PR.</p>

Principle Where How Single responsibility <code>activities()</code> vs its list callers; the exporter; <code>reloadAfterSetoranChange</code> The lookup returns every row and the lists choose the counted ones. The exporter formats a report and doesn't publish keys. One helper owns the reload set, and the dialog only collects the alasan and sends it. Open/closed <code>activity_sources</code> The rule sits in the shared source query, so a new consumer of the feed (a new export, a new total) gets it without being edited. Liskov substitution <code>TransaksiQuerySet</code> returned from <code>activities()</code> and <code>get_queryset</code> It's a <code>QuerySet[Transaksi]</code>, so every existing caller works unchanged, while the list callers can now ask for <code>.tercatat()</code>. Interface segregation List endpoints vs the detail lookup List consumers ask for the counted subset explicitly. The detail, edit and void paths keep an interface that still includes voided rows, because they need them. Dependency inversion The dialog → <code>reloadAfterSetoranChange(ProviderContainer)</code> The dialog depends on the provider container it is given, not on which screens exist. Tests pass their own container with a stub API and read the providers back. lib/features/transaksi/presentation/widgets/batalkan_setoran_dialog.dart<pre><code>final container = ProviderScope.containerOf(context, listen: false);
...
container.read(aktivitasSelectionProvider.notifier).clear();
reloadAfterSetoranChange(container);
</code></pre>

