Step Commit Result Red <code>b10fffa</code> <code>test_counted_setoran_are_read_through_tercatat</code> fails on exactly one line: <code>apps/reporting/services.py:100</code> Green <code>8d1a931</code> <code>waste_categories</code> reads through <code>tercatat()</code>; the existing PIL-428 behaviour test still sees one deposit after a void tests/test_architecture.py<pre><code>def test_counted_setoran_are_read_through_tercatat(self) -&gt; None:
    violations: list[str] = []
    for path in sorted(APPS_ROOT.rglob("*.py")):
        if path == TERCATAT_RULE_HOME or path.name.startswith("test_"):
            continue
        violations.extend(
            f"{path.relative_to(REPO_ROOT)}:{line}"
            for line in _spelled_out_tercatat_filters(path)
        )
    self.assertEqual(violations, [])
</code></pre> <p><code>_spelled_out_tercatat_filters</code> walks the syntax tree for <code>.filter()</code> and <code>.exclude()</code> calls whose keyword names <code>Transaksi.Status.TERCATAT</code> or ends in <code>transaksi__status</code>. A test that greps text would be fooled by a comment. This one is not, and because it failed on exactly the line in question, it isn't vacuous.</p> <p>The green commit is named <code>refactor(reporting): [GREEN]</code>: it makes the test pass without changing behaviour, which the unchanged PIL-428 test shows.</p>

lib/features/bank_sampah_approval/presentation/pages/approval_bank_sampah_list_page.dart<pre><code>/// PIL-539: the registration form, opened in-app for an account that
/// already has a membership. A submitted application pops `true`, and the
/// new one is pending, so the list is reloaded to show it.
void _applyToAnotherBank(BuildContext context, WidgetRef ref) {
  context.push&lt;bool&gt;(RegisterNasabahScreen.additionalRoute).then((applied) {
